The operations request is not included in this code. This node can only call `aap:caps/inference-llm`, and the target has no WASI adapter, so there is no filesystem to append `/var/log/aap/node-inputs.log` to. The enrichment fetch would also put the untrusted feed text into a URL sent to an outside service. That would be a new data flow the node's declaration doesn't allow. Both would need to be added to the graph, for example as a separate node holding `HTTPClient<[metadata.internal.example]>` or a log/state handle, before any body could do them.

